      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the prime factorization of 342.\n2. Determine the prime factorization of 285.\n3. Identify the common factors of 342 and 285.\n4. The largest common factor is the largest divisor that meets the criteria.\n\nLet's start with the prime factorization of 342:\n\\[ 342 \\div 2 = 171 \\]\n\\[ 171 \\div 3 = 57 \\]\n\\[ 57 \\div 3 = 19 \\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n\\[ 342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19 \\]\n\nNext, let's determine the prime factorization of 285:\n\\[ 285 \\div 3 = 95 \\]\n\\[ 95 \\div 5 = 19 \\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n\\[ 285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19 \\]\n\nNow, we identify the common factors of 342 and 285. The common prime factors are 3 and 19. Therefore, the common factor is:\n\\[ 3 \\times 19 = 57 \\]\n\nTo verify, we can check if 57 divides both 342 and 285:\n\\[ 342 \\div 57 = 6 \\]\n\\[ 285 \\div 57 = 5 \\]\nBoth divisions are exact, confirming that 57 is a common factor.\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{57} \\]",
